# Machine+OS port directory.  glibc's sysdeps search only recognises an OS
# through a machine/os directory like this one; the shared OS pieces live in
# sysdeps/unix/sysv/zhaoxu and the x86_64 tree supplies the machine code.
# The nptl subdirectories are normally pulled in by the Linux port, so the
# zhaoxu port lists them explicitly (TLS block layout, pthread types).
unix/sysv/zhaoxu
x86/nptl
x86_64/64/nptl
x86_64/nptl
x86_64
